opencl: cl_khr_d3d11_sharing copies through OpenCL-owned host memory, never the D3D11 mapping (Neutron#47 on ROCm)

What the reporter saw (Neutron#47, AMD RX 7600 XT, RADV + ROCm OpenCL "gfx1102", runtime 11.10-172.1 = 172 + 135): with the
sharing on, After Effects shows no layer controls and a black Draft 3D. On the reporter's machine our conformance exe (82 checks)
gave 66 pass / 16 fail: every image check fails in both directions and every format (first wrong texel 0,0; frames
"row 0 stale or wrong"; Texture3D both ways); every buffer check and every error-code check passes.

Mechanism (INFERRED -- not reproduced in the lab, see below):
- 135's acquire handed the pointer from ID3D11DeviceContext::Map of a staging resource (memory of the Vulkan driver
  behind DXVK, here RADV on the same GPU) and D3D11's RowPitch straight to a blocking clEnqueueWriteImage; release
  did the same with clEnqueueReadImage. That is legal OpenCL (blocking_write CL_TRUE: the implementation copies the
  data at ptr before returning; input_row_pitch may be any value >= width * element size). What an implementation
  does with such a pointer is its own business. ROCm's runtime (ROCclr, from its design, not traced on the reporter's machine)
  pins host pointers for image transfers and falls back to a staged path when it cannot; another driver's BO mapping
  cannot be pinned, so our transfers and the application's own likely took different ROCm paths. In the reporter's output every
  failing check has a host image transfer in it, while the kernel-only round trip (acquire -> kernel -> release) of the
  4-channel formats was right except row 0 (the 1-channel ones prove nothing there: that kernel's output ignores them).
- Not the 135 hypotheses: no non-blocking transfer on a mapped pointer (all were CL_TRUE), no USE_HOST_PTR /
  COPY_HOST_PTR images, and the events returned are markers after the completed copies.

Windows: AMD's and Intel's drivers implement the extension natively (the shared object IS the D3D11 resource); the
copies are ours, so the rule is ours to choose: the OpenCL implementation only ever touches memory it allocated.

Fix (dlls/opencl/pe_d3d11.c, PE side only):
- every shared object gets a host buffer (clCreateBuffer CL_MEM_ALLOC_HOST_PTR, tightly packed, element size from
  CL_IMAGE_ELEMENT_SIZE), created on first use, freed with the object.
- acquire: D3D11 resource -> staging (CopySubresourceRegion + Map READ, as before) -> CPU copy row by row (D3D11
  pitches) into the host buffer mapped with a blocking clEnqueueMapBuffer(CL_MAP_WRITE_INVALIDATE_REGION) -> unmap ->
  clEnqueueCopyBufferToImage / clEnqueueCopyBuffer into the shared object, after the application's wait list AND the
  unmap's event (so out-of-order queues are right: a buffer mapped for writing must be unmapped before a command reads
  it) -> wait for the copy.
- release: clEnqueueCopyImageToBuffer / clEnqueueCopyBuffer after the application's wait list -> blocking map
  (CL_MAP_READ) that waits for that copy -> CPU copy into the D3D11 mapping (its pitches) -> Unmap +
  CopySubresourceRegion back (DYNAMIC: Map WRITE_DISCARD directly, as before) -> unmap the host buffer, waited.
- both still complete when the call returns (also covers CL_CONTEXT_INTEROP_USER_SYNC), so nothing else changes:
  the returned event is the same marker, the host buffer is idle between calls.
- Kill switch NEUTRON_CL_D3D11_DIRECT_COPY=1: 135's direct transfers (for an A/B on one build).

Not covered: the lab has no AMD GPU, so this is proven correct on two other implementations, not proven to fix ROCm.
If plain OpenCL images are wrong on the reporter's ROCm under Wine as well (no sharing code involved), that is a separate bug:
conformance exe v2 (cl11b/test) has "control:" checks for exactly that, plus `ab` (both copy paths in one run).
Zero copy (Vulkan external memory) is still a later step.

Lab evidence (cl11b, 11-06):
- No repro of the failure: 135's copies pass on NVIDIA 615.78 (RTX 5070) and on Mesa 26.2.6 rusticl (llvmpipe, device
  type forced GPU) + DXVK on lavapipe in a GPU-less container: clcore conformance 82/82, n=2 each, same build.
- This patch, runtime 11.10-172.3t (= 172.1 + this opencl.dll), same build A/B: clcore conformance (82 checks) fix 82/82
  x2 and kill switch 82/82 x2 on NVIDIA; fix 82/82 x2 and kill 82/82 x2 on rusticl. Conformance v2 (93 checks: + 5
  plain-image controls + 6 kernel-read checks, validated against a deliberately broken build: 7 FAIL) with `ab`: 93/93
  both arms, NVIDIA x2 (and on 172.1), rusticl x2.
- After Effects 26.5 Advanced 3D on the OpenCL spoof (claex method, AeB1, 182x1 + this lab dll), fix vs kill on one
  build, n=1 each: CALDER-SUPPORTED, renderer stays Calder, renders pixel-identical to 135's (mean |d| 0.00, 0% px),
  viewer fix vs kill 0.00% px; 400 acquires + 400 releases, no errors.
- Cost (AE, same build): acquire avg 3.13 ms vs 2.46 ms, release 2.01 ms vs 1.51 ms => ~10.3 vs ~7.9 ms per displayed
  frame (2 acquires + 2 releases). Conformance 1080p RGBA8 acquire 2.0 vs 1.6 ms (NVIDIA), 3.7 vs 2.4 ms (rusticl);
  with another thread hammering the immediate context 23 vs 11 ms (NVIDIA).

--- a/dlls/opencl/pe_d3d11.c	2026-11-06 15:52:26.969916287 -0500
+++ b/dlls/opencl/pe_d3d11.c	2026-11-06 15:52:26.970916322 -0500
@@ -28,6 +28,12 @@
  * - a shared memory object is a host buffer or image of the same size and format as the D3D11 (sub)resource;
  * - acquire copies the D3D11 contents into it (through a staging resource on the application's D3D11 device) and
  *   release copies them back, both complete when the call returns, which also covers CL_CONTEXT_INTEROP_USER_SYNC;
+ * - the OpenCL implementation only ever sees memory it allocated itself: the D3D11 mapping is copied into (or out of)
+ *   a host buffer of the shared object's context (CL_MEM_ALLOC_HOST_PTR, tightly packed, mapped with
+ *   clEnqueueMapBuffer), and that buffer is copied to the shared object on the device. A D3D11 Map pointer is memory
+ *   of the Vulkan driver behind D3D11; handing it to clEnqueueWriteImage/ReadImage (with D3D11's row pitch) is legal
+ *   OpenCL but leaves the result to how each implementation pins or stages foreign host memory, and ROCm (Neutron#47)
+ *   got every image transfer wrong that way. NEUTRON_CL_D3D11_DIRECT_COPY=1 goes back to the direct transfers;
  * - OpenCL devices are matched to DXGI adapters by PCI location (Vulkan, through DXVK's interop interface, against
  *   cl_khr_pci_bus_info or the vendor's own device queries), then by device UUID, then by vendor.
  *
@@ -113,6 +119,8 @@
     UINT subresource;
     size_t size, width, height, depth;
     ID3D11Resource *staging;
+    cl_mem host_buffer;           /* CL_MEM_ALLOC_HOST_PTR, tightly packed copy of the object, see copy_to_host */
+    size_t element_size;          /* bytes per texel (1 for buffers) */
     BOOL acquired;
     BOOL released;
 };
@@ -190,6 +198,20 @@
     return enabled;
 }
 
+/* the copies of 135 straight from and to the D3D11 mapping, for an A/B on one build */
+static BOOL direct_copy_enabled(void)
+{
+    static int enabled = -1;
+
+    if (enabled == -1)
+    {
+        const char *env = getenv( "NEUTRON_CL_D3D11_DIRECT_COPY" );
+        enabled = env && *env == '1';
+        if (enabled) WARN( "NEUTRON_CL_D3D11_DIRECT_COPY: transfers straight from and to the D3D11 mapping\n" );
+    }
+    return enabled;
+}
+
 static cl_int host_device_info( cl_device_id device, cl_device_info name, size_t size, void *value )
 {
     struct clGetDeviceInfo_params params = { device, name, size, value, NULL };
@@ -462,6 +484,7 @@
     {
         TRACE( "freeing memory object %p\n", mem->mem );
         if (mem->staging) ID3D11Resource_Release( mem->staging );
+        if (mem->host_buffer) host_release_mem( mem->host_buffer );
         ID3D11Resource_Release( mem->resource );
         host_release_mem( mem->mem );
         InterlockedDecrement( &d3d11_objects );
@@ -835,6 +858,14 @@
     if (!ret && !handle_mem) ret = CL_OUT_OF_RESOURCES;
     if (ret) goto done;
 
+    mem->element_size = 1;
+    if (dimension != D3D11_RESOURCE_DIMENSION_BUFFER)
+    {
+        struct clGetImageInfo_params params = { handle_mem, CL_IMAGE_ELEMENT_SIZE, sizeof(mem->element_size),
+                                                &mem->element_size, NULL };
+        if ((ret = OPENCL_CALL( clGetImageInfo, &params ))) goto done;
+    }
+
     {
         /* the reference that keeps the object, and our record of it, alive until we free it */
         struct clRetainMemObject_params params = { handle_mem };
@@ -998,8 +1029,9 @@
     }
 }
 
-/* acquire: D3D11 resource -> staging -> host object */
-static cl_int copy_to_host( cl_command_queue queue, struct d3d11_mem *mem, cl_uint num_events, const cl_event *events )
+/* NEUTRON_CL_D3D11_DIRECT_COPY=1 (135's copies) -- acquire: D3D11 resource -> staging -> host object */
+static cl_int copy_to_host_direct( cl_command_queue queue, struct d3d11_mem *mem, cl_uint num_events,
+                                   const cl_event *events )
 {
     struct d3d11_context *context = mem->context;
     D3D11_MAPPED_SUBRESOURCE map;
@@ -1027,8 +1059,9 @@
     return ret;
 }
 
-/* release: host object -> staging -> D3D11 resource; a dynamic resource takes the data directly */
-static cl_int copy_from_host( cl_command_queue queue, struct d3d11_mem *mem, cl_uint num_events, const cl_event *events )
+/* NEUTRON_CL_D3D11_DIRECT_COPY=1 (135's copies) -- release: host object -> staging -> D3D11 resource */
+static cl_int copy_from_host_direct( cl_command_queue queue, struct d3d11_mem *mem, cl_uint num_events,
+                                     const cl_event *events )
 {
     struct d3d11_context *context = mem->context;
     BOOL dynamic = mem->usage == D3D11_USAGE_DYNAMIC;
@@ -1061,6 +1094,236 @@
     return ret;
 }
 
+static size_t host_buffer_size( const struct d3d11_mem *mem )
+{
+    if (mem->dimension == D3D11_RESOURCE_DIMENSION_BUFFER) return mem->size;
+    return mem->width * mem->height * mem->depth * mem->element_size;
+}
+
+static cl_int create_host_buffer( struct d3d11_mem *mem )
+{
+    cl_int ret = CL_SUCCESS;
+    struct clCreateBuffer_params params = { &mem->host_buffer, mem->context->context,
+                                            CL_MEM_READ_WRITE | CL_MEM_ALLOC_HOST_PTR, host_buffer_size( mem ), NULL,
+                                            &ret };
+
+    OPENCL_CALL( clCreateBuffer, &params );
+    if (!ret && !mem->host_buffer) ret = CL_OUT_OF_RESOURCES;
+    if (ret)
+    {
+        ERR( "failed to create a host buffer of %Iu bytes for %p, error %d\n", host_buffer_size( mem ),
+             mem->app_resource, ret );
+        mem->host_buffer = NULL;
+    }
+    return ret;
+}
+
+static void release_event( cl_event event )
+{
+    struct clReleaseEvent_params params = { event };
+    if (event) OPENCL_CALL( clReleaseEvent, &params );
+}
+
+/* waits for the command, then drops our reference to its event */
+static cl_int wait_event( cl_event event )
+{
+    struct clWaitForEvents_params wait = { 1, &event };
+    cl_int status = CL_COMPLETE, ret;
+    struct clGetEventInfo_params info = { event, CL_EVENT_COMMAND_EXECUTION_STATUS, sizeof(status), &status, NULL };
+
+    ret = OPENCL_CALL( clWaitForEvents, &wait );
+    if (!ret && !OPENCL_CALL( clGetEventInfo, &info ) && status < 0) ret = status;
+    release_event( event );
+    return ret;
+}
+
+/* blocking map of the whole host buffer, after the command of event (if any); the host buffer is idle otherwise:
+ * every command on it is complete before acquire or release returns */
+static void *map_host_buffer( cl_command_queue queue, struct d3d11_mem *mem, cl_map_flags flags, cl_event event,
+                              cl_int *ret )
+{
+    void *ptr = NULL;
+    struct clEnqueueMapBuffer_params params = { &ptr, queue, mem->host_buffer, CL_TRUE, flags, 0,
+                                                host_buffer_size( mem ), event ? 1 : 0, event ? &event : NULL,
+                                                NULL, ret };
+
+    OPENCL_CALL( clEnqueueMapBuffer, &params );
+    if (!*ret && !ptr) *ret = CL_MAP_FAILURE;
+    return *ret ? NULL : ptr;
+}
+
+static cl_int unmap_host_buffer( cl_command_queue queue, struct d3d11_mem *mem, void *ptr, cl_event *event )
+{
+    struct clEnqueueUnmapMemObject_params params = { queue, mem->host_buffer, ptr, 0, NULL, event };
+
+    return OPENCL_CALL( clEnqueueUnmapMemObject, &params );
+}
+
+/* the D3D11 mapping has its own row and depth pitches, the host buffer is tightly packed */
+static void copy_rows( const struct d3d11_mem *mem, const D3D11_MAPPED_SUBRESOURCE *map, BYTE *host, BOOL to_host )
+{
+    size_t row_size = mem->width * mem->element_size, y, z;
+    BYTE *d3d11, *cl;
+
+    if (mem->dimension == D3D11_RESOURCE_DIMENSION_BUFFER)
+    {
+        if (to_host) memcpy( host, map->pData, mem->size );
+        else memcpy( map->pData, host, mem->size );
+        return;
+    }
+    for (z = 0; z < mem->depth; z++)
+    {
+        for (y = 0; y < mem->height; y++)
+        {
+            d3d11 = (BYTE *)map->pData + z * map->DepthPitch + y * map->RowPitch;
+            cl = host + (z * mem->height + y) * row_size;
+            if (to_host) memcpy( cl, d3d11, row_size );
+            else memcpy( d3d11, cl, row_size );
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/* host buffer -> shared object on the device, after the application's wait list and the unmap of the host buffer;
+ * complete when this returns */
+static cl_int copy_host_buffer_to_mem( cl_command_queue queue, struct d3d11_mem *mem, cl_uint num_events,
+                                       const cl_event *events, cl_event unmapped )
+{
+    size_t origin[3] = {0, 0, 0}, region[3] = {mem->width, mem->height, mem->depth};
+    cl_event event = NULL, *wait;
+    cl_int ret;
+
+    if (!(wait = malloc( (num_events + 1) * sizeof(*wait) ))) return CL_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY;
+    if (num_events) memcpy( wait, events, num_events * sizeof(*wait) );
+    wait[num_events] = unmapped;
+
+    if (mem->dimension == D3D11_RESOURCE_DIMENSION_BUFFER)
+    {
+        struct clEnqueueCopyBuffer_params params = { queue, mem->host_buffer, mem->mem, 0, 0, mem->size,
+                                                     num_events + 1, wait, &event };
+        ret = OPENCL_CALL( clEnqueueCopyBuffer, &params );
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        struct clEnqueueCopyBufferToImage_params params = { queue, mem->host_buffer, mem->mem, 0, origin, region,
+                                                            num_events + 1, wait, &event };
+        ret = OPENCL_CALL( clEnqueueCopyBufferToImage, &params );
+    }
+    free( wait );
+    if (ret) return ret;
+    return wait_event( event );
+}
+
+/* shared object -> host buffer, after the application's wait list */
+static cl_int copy_mem_to_host_buffer( cl_command_queue queue, struct d3d11_mem *mem, cl_uint num_events,
+                                       const cl_event *events, cl_event *event )
+{
+    size_t origin[3] = {0, 0, 0}, region[3] = {mem->width, mem->height, mem->depth};
+
+    if (mem->dimension == D3D11_RESOURCE_DIMENSION_BUFFER)
+    {
+        struct clEnqueueCopyBuffer_params params = { queue, mem->mem, mem->host_buffer, 0, 0, mem->size,
+                                                     num_events, events, event };
+        return OPENCL_CALL( clEnqueueCopyBuffer, &params );
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        struct clEnqueueCopyImageToBuffer_params params = { queue, mem->mem, mem->host_buffer, origin, region, 0,
+                                                            num_events, events, event };
+        return OPENCL_CALL( clEnqueueCopyImageToBuffer, &params );
+    }
+}
+
+/* acquire: D3D11 resource -> staging -> (CPU) host buffer -> (device copy) shared object */
+static cl_int copy_to_host( cl_command_queue queue, struct d3d11_mem *mem, cl_uint num_events, const cl_event *events )
+{
+    struct d3d11_context *context = mem->context;
+    D3D11_MAPPED_SUBRESOURCE map;
+    cl_event unmapped = NULL;
+    cl_int ret;
+    void *host;
+    HRESULT hr;
+
+    if (direct_copy_enabled()) return copy_to_host_direct( queue, mem, num_events, events );
+    if (!mem->staging && FAILED(create_staging( mem ))) return CL_OUT_OF_RESOURCES;
+    if (!mem->host_buffer && (ret = create_host_buffer( mem ))) return ret;
+
+    if (!(host = map_host_buffer( queue, mem, CL_MAP_WRITE_INVALIDATE_REGION, NULL, &ret )))
+    {
+        ERR( "failed to map the host buffer of %p, error %d\n", mem->app_resource, ret );
+        return ret;
+    }
+
+    lock_d3d11( context );
+    ID3D11DeviceContext_CopySubresourceRegion( context->immediate, mem->staging, 0, 0, 0, 0,
+                                               mem->resource, mem->subresource, NULL );
+    hr = ID3D11DeviceContext_Map( context->immediate, mem->staging, 0, D3D11_MAP_READ, 0, &map );
+    unlock_d3d11( context );
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr))
+    {
+        copy_rows( mem, &map, host, TRUE );
+        lock_d3d11( context );
+        ID3D11DeviceContext_Unmap( context->immediate, mem->staging, 0 );
+        unlock_d3d11( context );
+    }
+    else ERR( "failed to map the staging resource of %p, hr %#lx\n", mem->app_resource, hr );
+
+    if ((ret = unmap_host_buffer( queue, mem, host, &unmapped ))) return ret;
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr)) ret = copy_host_buffer_to_mem( queue, mem, num_events, events, unmapped );
+    else ret = CL_OUT_OF_RESOURCES;
+    /* the copy ran after the unmap; without a copy, wait for the unmap itself */
+    if (ret) wait_event( unmapped );
+    else release_event( unmapped );
+    return ret;
+}
+
+/* release: shared object -> (device copy) host buffer -> (CPU) staging -> D3D11 resource; a dynamic resource takes
+ * the data directly */
+static cl_int copy_from_host( cl_command_queue queue, struct d3d11_mem *mem, cl_uint num_events, const cl_event *events )
+{
+    struct d3d11_context *context = mem->context;
+    BOOL dynamic = mem->usage == D3D11_USAGE_DYNAMIC;
+    ID3D11Resource *target = dynamic ? mem->resource : mem->staging;
+    UINT target_sub = dynamic ? mem->subresource : 0;
+    D3D11_MAPPED_SUBRESOURCE map;
+    cl_event copied = NULL, unmapped = NULL;
+    cl_int ret;
+    void *host;
+    HRESULT hr;
+
+    if (direct_copy_enabled()) return copy_from_host_direct( queue, mem, num_events, events );
+    if (!target) return CL_OUT_OF_RESOURCES;
+    if (!mem->host_buffer && (ret = create_host_buffer( mem ))) return ret;
+
+    if ((ret = copy_mem_to_host_buffer( queue, mem, num_events, events, &copied ))) return ret;
+    /* blocking: the copy is complete when the map returns */
+    host = map_host_buffer( queue, mem, CL_MAP_READ, copied, &ret );
+    release_event( copied );
+    if (!host)
+    {
+        ERR( "failed to map the host buffer of %p, error %d\n", mem->app_resource, ret );
+        return ret;
+    }
+
+    lock_d3d11( context );
+    hr = ID3D11DeviceContext_Map( context->immediate, target, target_sub,
+                                  dynamic ? D3D11_MAP_WRITE_DISCARD : D3D11_MAP_WRITE, 0, &map );
+    unlock_d3d11( context );
+    if (SUCCEEDED(hr))
+    {
+        copy_rows( mem, &map, host, FALSE );
+        lock_d3d11( context );
+        ID3D11DeviceContext_Unmap( context->immediate, target, target_sub );
+        if (!dynamic)
+            ID3D11DeviceContext_CopySubresourceRegion( context->immediate, mem->resource, mem->subresource, 0, 0, 0,
+                                                       mem->staging, 0, NULL );
+        unlock_d3d11( context );
+    }
+    else ERR( "failed to map %p for writing, hr %#lx\n", mem->app_resource, hr );
+
+    if (!(ret = unmap_host_buffer( queue, mem, host, &unmapped ))) ret = wait_event( unmapped );
+    return FAILED(hr) ? CL_OUT_OF_RESOURCES : ret;
+}
+
 static cl_int enqueue_d3d11_objects( cl_command_queue queue, cl_uint num_objects, const cl_mem *mem_objects,
                                      cl_uint num_events, const cl_event *events, cl_event *event, BOOL acquire )
 {
